WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.085
Dame Kristin.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.295
Dame Kristin.

00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:05.296
Are we not having an interview?

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:07.549
No, it's just, we're having a chat.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:08.800
The way we do.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.634
Like we do.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:13.680
Ladies and Gentlemen, Kristin Scott Thomas.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:20.687
Here we are, working again.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.691
You alone?

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:26.901
We go way back, don't we?

00:00:26.901 --> 00:00:28.820
Oh, we do. We do.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:34.492
Slow Horses is not casinos, champagne, and Aston Martins.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:37.537
It's such the other side of James Bond, isn't it?

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:41.291
No, totally. Behind-the-mirror kind of James Bond isn't it.

00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:43.501
It's the sort of stuff that you'd rather not look at.

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:44.461
Come see this!

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:45.378
Hostage.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.046
What's it got to do with you?

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.883
Whatever's going on will be a job for the real agents.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.093
It really has tongue in his cheek.

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:55.263
Personnellement, as the French would say, I really enjoy.

00:00:55.263 --> 00:00:56.306
As the French would say.

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:57.891
As the French would say.

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:00.685
What are you looking for?

00:01:00.977 --> 00:01:02.729
He hasn't told me yet what I'm looking for.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.022
Slough House is filthy!

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:07.275
You end up at Slow House and it's
a disgusting place, I mean…

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:08.693
It's interesting, you said, "Slow House."

00:01:08.693 --> 00:01:10.695
Did I say Slow House?
Slough House! 

00:01:10.695 --> 00:01:13.323
But it is slow house too, isn't it? It's "Slow House".

00:01:15.617 --> 00:01:17.827
Or we can sit here and watch the slow horses,

00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:21.664
walk in one by one and accept
a job back here at the park,

00:01:21.664 --> 00:01:24.000
while you fester in the basement.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.836
If you don't take this too personally.

00:01:26.836 --> 00:01:27.962
Brace.

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:31.299
You're very good at playing a tough…

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:32.217
Tough cookie?

00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:32.842
Yeah.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:34.469
I don't know where I get it from.

00:01:34.469 --> 00:01:35.637
I don't know.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:44.562
I've never seen anyone like
Jackson Lamb on my television before.

00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:45.104
No.

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:48.191
Anyone with me tonight is fireproof.

00:01:48.191 --> 00:01:51.152
God, you really care about them, don't you?

00:01:52.362 --> 00:01:54.948
Nah, I think they're a bunch of absolute losers.

00:01:55.156 --> 00:01:56.658
But they're my losers.

00:01:56.825 --> 00:02:00.328
The Taverner, Lamb scenes are particularly juicy.

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:03.790
It always feels like a relief when you
know that you've got a scene with Gary.

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:06.042
I mean, they were great to act.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:09.963
They bicker. They're almost like old lovers.
Like very old marriage.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:11.422
What do you think you're playing at?

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:12.799
What do you think you're playing at?

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:14.425
Do you think they enjoy it a bit?

00:02:14.843 --> 00:02:18.972
I think they enjoy it a bit, and they've
learned to live with each other.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:25.061
The dread is always sort of overtaken by this joy
that they get from this little, sort of, spark.

00:02:25.061 --> 00:02:28.815
In three seconds, I could have a
dozen guns pointed at your head.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.650
Yeah, but you won't do that.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.651
It's fun to do!

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.363
You have actors you can play tennis with.

00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:38.157
Yeah, you can rely on to surpise you and

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.535
send the ball back but in a surprising manner.
Absolutely.

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:41.744
That's really exciting, isn't it?

00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:45.874
When I learned that Slow Horses
was coming together

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:47.208
I was thrilled.

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.460
I was thinking, oh that be great
to work with Kristin

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.463
Yeah. It's just so surprising
in its twists and turns.

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:53.715
And the characters.

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:55.633
Characters. Characters are great.
It's just so interesting.

00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:58.636
You probably know how many people
have made it back from Slough House

00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:00.638
to upstairs here at Regent's Park.

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:04.350
It's Saturday. Haven't you got other
peoples cats to steal?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.059
None.

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:06.311
Thank you for joining us.

00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:07.896
Who are you talking to?
I can't tell... 

00:03:07.896 --> 00:03:09.522
I'm talking to the audience.
Oh.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.690
Our audience out there.

